message: >-
  Please cite this software/research artifact when referring to its implementation
  or synthetic results. Srinivas Nampalli and Saathvik Gampa are the document
  authors designated by the user. SrinivasNampalli is the project maintainer.
  The user reports equal 50/50 general technical contributions by the two authors.
  These attributions do not determine patent inventorship, applicant status,
  or ownership; dated and claim-specific contributions remain to be documented.
type: software
title: "Thermal Queue Governor: clipped sensing and delayed motor commands"
authors:
  - family-names: Nampalli
    given-names: Srinivas
  - family-names: Gampa
    given-names: Saathvik
contact:
  - name: SrinivasNampalli
    website: "https://github.com/SrinivasNampalli"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SrinivasNampalli/thermal-queue-governor"
url: "https://srinivasnampalli.github.io/thermal-queue-governor/"
version: 0.3.0
abstract: >-
  AI-assisted synthetic research and interactive software for a scalar interval
  motor thermal governor with clipped observations and an accepted-command FIFO.
  Results are conditional on the stated model and actuator assumptions.
  Motor-specific virtual validation is pending the user's selected motor
  specifications. Generic software tests verify code, not a named motor;
  no held-out motor data run, hardware validation, or patent filing is claimed.
  Original materials remain rights reserved pending review; third-party
  dependencies retain their licenses.
keywords:
  - thermal control
  - interval estimation
  - motor control
  - clipped sensors
  - command governor
